<title>MALAYSIA: Berjaya Leisure unit plans shop complex.</title>
<headline>Berjaya Leisure unit plans shop complex.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cempaka Properties Sdn Bhd, a subsidiary of Berjaya Leisure Bhd, is developing a 500-million ringgit shopping and hotel complex in the east coast city of Kuantan, the national Bernama news agency said.</p>
<p>Its general manager Lim Kiu Hock was quoted as saying on Wednesday that the 18-hectare site will included shoplots, a shopping mall and a hotel.</p>
<p>The seven-storey 150 million ringgit shopping mall itself is expected to open in October 1997, he added.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
